      "analysis": "Price action: US30 ground lower for the 3rd consecutive week in a near-uninterrupted 10-session decline. The FOMC decision produced no relief rally — the index gapped from 52,093 to a 51,462 low before a weak bounce to 51,778. Friday closed at 51,683. Structure is a clean series of lower highs/lows since the 53,686 Sep 3 peak. Fundamentals: Fed +25bp to 3.75-4.00%. 55.4% probability of October hike. 10Y at 5% is a valuation headwind for the Dow's industrial/cyclical composition. USD +1.1% creates currency translation drag. Outlook: 3-day NEUTRAL-BEARISH. Sell rallies 52,000-52,100 stop 52,400 target 51,000. Below 51,462 opens 51,000."
